Subject: [PATCH] R82-2 v2 (cld-advisor, at main's word in M48 and M53, under
 main's rule of M41; register row P-881): A VERDICT LINE NAMES NO SEAT OTHER
 THAN MAIN: 79 LINES RE-WORDED, THE CREDIT IN cites_seat, AND A GATE WITH AN
 OPEN LIST OF NAMES

The 71 lines of 2026-11-26, with M53's corrections 1 and 2 (B1894's synonym now "a seat";
B1832's c4_test_keys_static.json left out). Correction 3: the gate reads its names from
scripts/gates/SEAT_NAMES.json, an open list; each word of a lane's name is read with lane, seat,
family and branches, so synonyms are read. The 18 lines that name a seat the closed list missed
(the physical lane, the explore seat, the independent audit lane, B1826's physical-bridge lane,
the building session named by its work), 8 of them not among the 71, re-worded the same way: 79
lines in all, each with a dated note and its credit in cites_seat. Four locks (B1889, B1893,
B1896, B1898) hold the new words. Tests probe synonyms, a name added to the list alone, and the
list gone (fail-closed).
