+## A verdict line names no seat other than main — GATED (`claim-names-no-session`) (adopted 2026-11-14, main's rule of M41 for Review 82's item R82-2; register row P-881; built by the building session at main's M48)
+
+**The rule:** a verdict line (`claim_one_line`) names, as a source, an authority or a subject, no seat other than main:
+not the agy lane or its seats, the web seat, the SM seat, the advisor seat or the building session, the audit lane, or
+codex. The credit stands in the verdict file's `cites_seat`, or as "the card in harvest row N"; main stays named. Not a
+name: a seat's item id (`sm:…`, `W…`), a name inside a quotation, a branch name, "the builder" meaning a script. **The
+gate** reads every verdict line from B1814 on; its failing paths are `tests/test_claim_names_no_session.py`.
+
+**Why it exists.** Review 82 found verdict lines that credit a session by name inside the claim. On 2026-11-26 the 71
+lines from B1814 on that did were re-worded, each with a dated note on its page naming the commit that holds it as it
+stood.
+
+**[CHANGED 2026-11-28 (main's M53, R82-2 v2):** the list of names is open. It stands in `scripts/gates/SEAT_NAMES.json`,
+which the gate reads: a seat's names as the record writes them, the words of the lanes' names, each read in every form
+"the <word> lane", "seat", "family" or "branches", and the ways the record names the building session by its work ("the
+builder of the gates", "the gates' builder"). A new seat is one line of the file, not an edit of the gate; with the file
+unreadable the gate fails. The closed list had missed the physical lane, the explore seat and the independent audit lane,
+and a synonym; the 18 lines they named from B1814 on (8 of them not among the 71) were re-worded the same way, each with
+a dated note. When the
+author's identity table of draft 1, section 8, exists, the gate reads its names from there.**]**
